{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1548887-expression","id":1548887,"title":"Expression:","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-03-02T12:52:17-08:00","id":1548887,"title":"Expression:","content":"This is a very important skill for any Uratha if they intend to at least pass as human, they need to be able to play the part. I call it, &quot;On Two's&quot; (vs. &quot;On Four's&quot;).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-03T02:15:52-08:00","id":1548898,"title":"","content":"Why do you say so?<br /> I mean, Uratha are all born human and, barring very low Harmony ratings are still in part humans.<br /> Why do you think they need to learn to &quot;pass&quot; as humans?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-03T09:17:55-08:00","id":1548908,"title":"","content":"In addition to what Neos said, Expression isn't a general &quot;being a person&quot; skill. (After all, otherwise wouldn't regular humans all have it pretty high?) It's art, performance, and composition. Being able to tell a rousing story is very useful for a Cahalith, but it's not usually necessary to prove to someone that you are a human and not some kind of alien being.<br /> <br /> Not really sure what the point of starting a new thread for this was either. What were we supposed to talk about?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-03T12:44:46-08:00","id":1548918,"title":"","content":"Also in addition: Socialize, Streetwise, and Subterfuge would like a word on what covers a character's ability to fit into social situations they're not normally inclined towards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-13T14:39:08-07:00","id":1549259,"title":"","content":"They're really only human until they hit puberty; acting can help them play the part of the form they are in; they have to pass as a normal human/wolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-13T16:25:10-07:00","id":1549274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1548887-expression?p=1549259#post1549259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're really only human until they hit puberty; acting can help them play the part of the form they are in; they have to pass as a normal human/wolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're human until they Change, and that really doesn't change the fact that Expression is the Skill for performance, and being able to play an instrument, write a speech, or act for the stage or the screen is not the go-to body of knowledge and practice for passing as a normal human, as Arms' post correctly highlights the more appropriate suspects in the lineup.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-13T16:40:57-07:00","id":1549275,"title":"","content":"I would think that having incredibly high Harmony ratings would be a prequiste to be able to interact with normal humans without raising suspicion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-14T05:47:22-07:00","id":1549294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1548887-expression?p=1549275#post1549275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would think that having incredibly high Harmony ratings would be a prequiste to be able to interact with normal humans...</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's more Humanity from Requiem. High Harmony isn't about being more human, it's about denying your nature as an uratha. So ironically the more you do it, the worse your ability to control yourself, because you're a werewolf whether you like it or not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...without raising suspicion. </div> </div> </div>How much of an issue is that? Like, most people in the CofD don't know about werewolves, so as long as you don't turn into one, then what's the problem?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-14T13:41:57-07:00","id":1549324,"title":"","content":"Yeah, if you look at the actual mechanics, very high Harmony turns you into David from <i>An American Werewolf in London</i>: someone desperately trying to deny what they are, but when the conditions are right, they turn into a violent monster that goes on a rampage and kills lots of people until he finally calms down and reverts to his human form. It doesn't end well because it doesn't take supernatural senses for other humans to figure out what's happening.<br /> <br /> Harmony 5 is where the Uratha are under the most control of their multilayered natures. They are balanced between flesh and spirit, wolf and human. This is the rating where the Uratha have the most control over their various instincts, and even if they do lose control have the most time to remove themselves from a situation before the worst case occurs. That said, being out of balance does have tempting perks as well. <br /> <br /> On top of this... the Uratha literally get a bonus to blending in to human society just by taking their human form. They are natural shapeshifters and their human form is a natural state for them. Acting normally human is part of being in a human shape for them (the same thing applies for them as wolves though there's a bit less of &quot;wolf society&quot; to deal with and more making sure humans and supernaturals think you're just a wolf).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-03T18:24:35-07:00","id":1549791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1548887-expression?p=1549274#post1549274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're human until they Change, and that really doesn't change the fact that Expression is the Skill for performance, and being able to play an instrument, write a speech, or act for the stage or the screen is not the go-to body of knowledge and practice for passing as a normal human, as Arms' post correctly highlights the more appropriate suspects in the lineup.</div> </div> </div> </div>What else could acting fall under?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-03T18:42:16-07:00","id":1549795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1548887-expression?p=1549791#post1549791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What else could acting fall under?</div> </div> </div> </div>The ones I pointed out that Heavy Arms had highlighted.<br /> <br /> The Chronicles of Darkness corebook's Skills section includes a short list of sample Contacts relating to each one, and the list for Subterfuge includes &quot;Out-of-work Actor.&quot; The Socialize Skill is likewise explicitly about being able to fit into a social situation (hence dots in it being a prerequisite for the Barfly Merit). The Streetwise Skill is generally applicable for working within the framework of the criminal underworld and other legal grey areas, including knowing how not to set off the wrong people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-04T00:07:27-07:00","id":1549807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1548887-expression?p=1549791#post1549791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What else could acting fall under?</div> </div> </div> </div>Acting generally falls under Expression, yes, but uratha posing as humans isn't <i>acting</i>. Acting is what you do on a stage. What you're talking about is <i>passing</i> which is a function of Socialize and/or Subterfuge (depending on the context; Empathy, Streetwise &amp; Politics could also help depending on what you want to pass as). Except rolling to pass as a human is unnecessary because uratha grew up as a human around humans and won't have any trouble passing as humans except in exceptional circumstances.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-04T11:13:09-07:00","id":1549819,"title":"","content":"The lupines are not like Prometheans who never were human to begin with and want to be mortal. Where as vampires, changelings, mages and werewolves started off as human beings before being altered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-05T21:13:22-07:00","id":1549860,"title":"","content":"The very idea that Uratha need any particular skill to pass as human is off. Plenty of humans lack those skills, plenty of humans feel weird to others, and yet they're not seen as anything other than human.<br /> <br /> What does an Uratha &quot;failing&quot; to pass as human looks like? How would people do or act like if they &quot;get&quot; that the Uratha doesn't pass as human? Why would anyone think that a given person is anything but human?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-06T02:50:07-07:00","id":1549866,"title":"","content":"A somewhat more realistic scenario for calling on a roll would be when more subtle aspects of an Uratha's nature might get noticed by someone actively watching them on a regular basis. Their innate regeneration, their increasing need to hunt and eat, popping on wolf senses even in Hishu for the perception bonus, etc. These are not usually difficult to explain away (and Hishu's Wolf In Sheep's Clothing ability makes it nearly impossible for casual passerby notice), but they can lead to an Uratha acting eccentric enough for a long term acquaintance to start questioning what's up with some of these eccentric behaviors (esp. as most of them get more noticeable over time as Primal Urge increases or Harmony sways too far in either direction).<br /> <br /> There's good reasons why Uratha that want to maintain a &quot;normal&quot; human style of living tend to fold jobs into the pack. This enables the core Uratha to have seemingly normal lives, with Wolf-blooded and trusted humans ensuring that there's a layer of distance between the werewolves and more skeptical humans that might ask too many questions about such quirky antics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-06T17:55:45-07:00","id":1549886,"title":"","content":"Yes, but even then no particular skill is important. Rather, any skill may come to play depending on the circumstances, or no skill at all but other arrangements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-06T18:39:50-07:00","id":1549888,"title":"","content":"For sure. I was just addressing the idea of what an Uratha failing to pass for human in a more normal game-play context would look like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}